WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.401 --> 00:00:02.535
-Our first guest tonight
is an Emmy-winning actress,

00:00:02.535 --> 00:00:04.003
producer, and director.

00:00:04.003 --> 00:00:07.073
Her new series, "The Gentle Art
of Swedish Death Cleaning,"

00:00:07.073 --> 00:00:08.841
is available
to stream on Peacock,

00:00:08.841 --> 00:00:11.110
and she's kicking off
her Restless Leg Tour

00:00:11.110 --> 00:00:13.512
alongside Tina Fey this weekend
in Washington, D.C.

00:00:13.512 --> 00:00:14.981
Please welcome back
to the show the one, the only,

00:00:14.981 --> 00:00:17.483
the best in the biz, our good
friend Amy Poehler, everybody.

00:00:17.483 --> 00:00:19.485
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:19.485 --> 00:00:40.506 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:40.506 --> 00:00:43.176
Welcome back.
-Hey, Seth!

00:00:43.176 --> 00:00:45.511
What a crowd!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:45.511 --> 00:00:48.081
-Look at this.
Look at the love.

00:00:48.081 --> 00:00:50.349
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Thank you.

00:00:50.349 --> 00:00:52.718
Thank you very much.

00:00:52.718 --> 00:00:55.721
-Now, I do not see you
barely enough anymore.

00:00:55.721 --> 00:00:57.356
-I know.
-But this has been a hot week

00:00:57.356 --> 00:00:59.659
because this is the second time
I've seen you this week.

00:00:59.659 --> 00:01:01.560
-Yeah.
-'Cause you are prepping

00:01:01.560 --> 00:01:03.363
for the Restless Leg Tour.
-Right.

00:01:03.363 --> 00:01:04.497
So we're getting ready
for our show.

00:01:04.497 --> 00:01:06.665
So you very kindly allowed me

00:01:06.665 --> 00:01:08.601
to come and practice
some stand-up here.

00:01:08.601 --> 00:01:10.770
-Yes. So we finished
taping on Tuesday,

00:01:10.770 --> 00:01:12.138
and then I got
to tell the audience,

00:01:12.138 --> 00:01:15.074
"Amy Poehler is gonna come out
and try stand-up jokes.

00:01:15.074 --> 00:01:17.677
-Yeah. And it was a hot crowd,
and I'm very nervous.

00:01:17.677 --> 00:01:19.546
I think it gave me
the confidence I didn't need.

00:01:19.546 --> 00:01:20.713
[ Laughter ]

00:01:20.713 --> 00:01:23.116
But, yeah, we're getting
ready to go out,

00:01:23.116 --> 00:01:24.650
and it was really fun
to practice it.

00:01:24.650 --> 00:01:27.187
And, you know, I don't want to
blow my stand-up on this show.

00:01:27.187 --> 00:01:28.621
-Yeah, of course.
-I want to get paid for it.

00:01:28.621 --> 00:01:32.024
-You have always said
your art is to get paid for.

00:01:32.024 --> 00:01:34.827
-I'm always like,
"My C material

00:01:34.827 --> 00:01:36.062
is what I'm going
to bring to this desk."

00:01:36.062 --> 00:01:37.997
-Gotcha.
So if you're watching this,

00:01:37.997 --> 00:01:39.332
if people at home
are watching this

00:01:39.332 --> 00:01:40.699
and they don't like the jokes,

00:01:40.699 --> 00:01:42.101
just know this is not
your best stuff.

00:01:42.101 --> 00:01:44.804
-I didn't even work on it.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:44.804 --> 00:01:46.973
Literally.
I think before, it was like,

00:01:46.973 --> 00:01:48.108
"What do you and Seth
want to talk about?"

00:01:48.108 --> 00:01:50.676
I was like, "Whatever."
[ Laughter ]

00:01:50.676 --> 00:01:53.313
But -- no, but I did talk
about a couple of things,

00:01:53.313 --> 00:01:54.847
and one of the things is that --

00:01:54.847 --> 00:01:56.448
how much I don't
like being pranked.

00:01:56.448 --> 00:01:57.483
-You have never let --

00:01:57.483 --> 00:01:59.619
And I believe
that people might think,

00:01:59.619 --> 00:02:02.722
"Oh, Amy's so fun.
She's an improviser.

00:02:02.722 --> 00:02:05.191
She loves being on her --
on her toes."

00:02:05.191 --> 00:02:07.126
You hate a prank.
You always have.

00:02:07.126 --> 00:02:09.829
-To me, if you throw me
a surprise party.

00:02:09.829 --> 00:02:11.064
You're not my friend.
Yeah.

00:02:11.064 --> 00:02:12.098
[ Laughter ]

00:02:12.098 --> 00:02:14.133
And I would just
turn around and walk out,

00:02:14.133 --> 00:02:16.135
and I'd say, "Lose my number."

00:02:16.135 --> 00:02:19.172
I'd scream, "Lose my number!"
to all my friends.

00:02:19.172 --> 00:02:20.539
And, you know, I think
sometimes people are like,

00:02:20.539 --> 00:02:22.275
"I don't like pranks,"
but they love pranks.

00:02:22.275 --> 00:02:23.442
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:02:23.442 --> 00:02:25.044
Well, the way you said it,
really made...

00:02:25.044 --> 00:02:28.447
-"I don't like -- I don't --
Don't prank me, don't prank me!"

00:02:28.447 --> 00:02:30.750
I really, really
don't like pranks.

00:02:30.750 --> 00:02:33.753
-Yeah, you remember --
It wasn't a prank, but we --

00:02:33.753 --> 00:02:35.889
When our dear friend,
producer of the show,

00:02:35.889 --> 00:02:37.991
Mike Shoemaker,
when he left "SNL,"

00:02:37.991 --> 00:02:39.726
we did a surprise party for him.

00:02:39.726 --> 00:02:41.227
And you and I
were working together.

00:02:41.227 --> 00:02:43.829
And this is how bad
you are at pranks, as well.

00:02:43.829 --> 00:02:46.098
-Yeah.
-You tried to text me,

00:02:46.098 --> 00:02:47.200
"Do you think Shoemaker knows

00:02:47.200 --> 00:02:48.267
we're throwing
a surprise party?"

00:02:48.267 --> 00:02:50.135
And who did you text instead?

00:02:50.135 --> 00:02:51.270
-Shoemaker.
-Yeah.

00:02:51.270 --> 00:02:52.938
[ Laughter ]

00:02:52.938 --> 00:02:55.774
So I think you internally
don't like pranks so much

00:02:55.774 --> 00:02:57.943
that you want to, like,
ruin them for other people.

00:02:57.943 --> 00:02:59.212
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:02:59.212 --> 00:03:03.649
-I always knew that Shoemaker
would want to know

00:03:03.649 --> 00:03:06.386
that there was a surprise party
being thrown, you know?

00:03:06.386 --> 00:03:09.155
And he's always
very nicely lied and said,

00:03:09.155 --> 00:03:10.590
"I don't even know
what that meant."

00:03:10.590 --> 00:03:14.193
And I was like, "It meant we
were having a surprise party,

00:03:14.193 --> 00:03:15.461
and I blew it."
[ Laughter ]

00:03:15.461 --> 00:03:17.396
Ugh!
That was a terrible moment.

00:03:17.396 --> 00:03:20.766
-Now, do you -- do you
consider magic in the same --

00:03:20.766 --> 00:03:22.101
-Yeah, I don't like magicians.

00:03:22.101 --> 00:03:24.937
I don't like magic.
I don't like anyone...

00:03:24.937 --> 00:03:26.606
I don't -- I don't --

00:03:26.606 --> 00:03:27.974
I don't [bleep] with magic.

00:03:27.974 --> 00:03:29.942
[ Laughter ]

00:03:29.942 --> 00:03:34.113
But I don't like, "Pick a card."
You know, "Pick a card."

00:03:34.113 --> 00:03:37.249
"No, pick someone else."
[ Laughter ]

00:03:37.249 --> 00:03:40.052
"Where did the card go?"

00:03:40.052 --> 00:03:41.753
I went into my car,
and I left

00:03:41.753 --> 00:03:44.357
because I hate -- I hate --
I don't like magicians.

00:03:44.357 --> 00:03:47.493
But I do think
that I was hypnotized

00:03:47.493 --> 00:03:49.562
without my consent
by a mentalist.

00:03:49.562 --> 00:03:51.163
-Really?
-Yeah.

00:03:51.163 --> 00:03:52.631
I've never told this story.
-Okay.

00:03:52.631 --> 00:03:55.301
-Because currently
there's a lawsuit pending.

00:03:55.301 --> 00:03:56.635
I'm just kidding.
But I was --

00:03:56.635 --> 00:03:58.504
[ Laughter ]
I was in London.

00:03:58.504 --> 00:04:02.108
Yes, I go to London
and travel.

00:04:02.108 --> 00:04:03.909
You're not the only one.
And I was in --

00:04:03.909 --> 00:04:05.177
-That's so weird, though,
'cause the other day,

00:04:05.177 --> 00:04:06.813
you were like,
"I don't like going to London."

00:04:06.813 --> 00:04:08.247
[ Laughter ]

00:04:08.247 --> 00:04:09.882
-So I was in the U.K.,

00:04:09.882 --> 00:04:12.117
and I was at a fancy dinner
many years ago.

00:04:12.117 --> 00:04:16.188
Tons of fancy people there,
expensive dinner, you know.

00:04:16.188 --> 00:04:17.657
-Oh, so at a proper restaurant.

00:04:17.657 --> 00:04:19.559
That's what
they say over there, "proper."

00:04:19.559 --> 00:04:20.960
-Oh, they do?
[ Laughter ]

00:04:20.960 --> 00:04:22.962
That's --
That's quite funny, Seth.

00:04:22.962 --> 00:04:24.730
[ Laughter ]

00:04:24.730 --> 00:04:27.399
And -- But, uh...

00:04:27.399 --> 00:04:29.302
I sit next to someone

00:04:29.302 --> 00:04:30.937
who is considered,
like, a mentalist.

00:04:30.937 --> 00:04:32.504
-Okay.
-Like, uh, you know,

00:04:32.504 --> 00:04:35.308
one of those weirdo freaks.
-Yeah, yeah.

00:04:35.308 --> 00:04:37.210
And if I had known that --
-That's a magician who's, like,

00:04:37.210 --> 00:04:41.214
bad at shuffling, right?
-Yeah. No card skills.

00:04:41.214 --> 00:04:42.915
But if I had known
he was like that,

00:04:42.915 --> 00:04:44.150
I would have never
sat next to him.

00:04:44.150 --> 00:04:47.119
I would have got a taxi or a...
-Black cab?

00:04:47.119 --> 00:04:49.555
-Black cab.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:49.555 --> 00:04:51.991
But at the end of the dinner,

00:04:51.991 --> 00:04:53.959
I stood up, and I was like,
"Dinner's on me,"

00:04:53.959 --> 00:04:55.461
and I remember everyone
being like, "Really?

00:04:55.461 --> 00:04:58.765
This is going to be like
£50,000 or whatever,"

00:04:58.765 --> 00:05:00.699
because they don't go
by dollars there.

00:05:00.699 --> 00:05:02.334
And, um...
[ Laughter ]

00:05:02.334 --> 00:05:04.337
I don't know if you know.
And --

00:05:04.337 --> 00:05:08.374
And I picked up the check,
and I went home, and I thought,

00:05:08.374 --> 00:05:10.642
"I think I was hypnotized."
[ Laughter ]

00:05:10.642 --> 00:05:12.211
I'm not kidding.
Have I ever told you this story?

00:05:12.211 --> 00:05:15.748
-No.
-I think that he was saying,

00:05:15.748 --> 00:05:18.217
like, "You should check
on your food

00:05:18.217 --> 00:05:20.720
and make sure it's picked up."

00:05:20.720 --> 00:05:24.223
Like, I think he touched me
in some weird way

00:05:24.223 --> 00:05:25.992
and he made me
pick up the check.

00:05:25.992 --> 00:05:28.928
-You think he mentalized you?
-Or...

00:05:28.928 --> 00:05:30.697
[ Laughter ]

00:05:30.697 --> 00:05:32.665
Or I was just trying
to big-time it.

00:05:32.665 --> 00:05:35.200
-Now, I will say I --
[ Laughter ]

00:05:35.200 --> 00:05:36.903
Because I have known you
to be a big-timer

00:05:36.903 --> 00:05:38.937
at fancy dinners.
-Yeah.

00:05:38.937 --> 00:05:40.239
-And it's one of
the great things about --

00:05:40.239 --> 00:05:42.174
There's one downside to it.

00:05:42.174 --> 00:05:44.043
It's great to be your friend
because the amount of times

00:05:44.043 --> 00:05:47.280
you will stand up and offer
to pay for dinner is the best.

00:05:47.280 --> 00:05:49.248
-Yeah.
-The bad side is how often

00:05:49.248 --> 00:05:50.850
you then realize
you don't have your wallet.

00:05:50.850 --> 00:05:52.918
-That's right.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:52.918 --> 00:05:56.288
That's right. At least --
At least 4 or 5 times.

00:05:56.288 --> 00:05:59.158
I have made a big --
-Big show.

00:05:59.158 --> 00:06:01.561
-A big show.
-Like, you wanted to get up.

00:06:01.561 --> 00:06:03.462
So you wanted to make sure
the rest of the table

00:06:03.462 --> 00:06:06.031
didn't hear it by word of mouth.
You wanted everyone to hear.

00:06:06.031 --> 00:06:07.800
-That's right.
-"Poehler's got it."

00:06:07.800 --> 00:06:09.201
-"I got it, guys,"
and people would be like,

00:06:09.201 --> 00:06:10.669
"Come on, no way,"
and I'd be like,

00:06:10.669 --> 00:06:12.738
"Ye-- Uh --
Let me take care of this."

00:06:12.738 --> 00:06:14.307
-You're like,
"You all work hard."

00:06:14.307 --> 00:06:17.743
-Exactly. And then I'd say,
"Oh, I don't have my wallet."

00:06:17.743 --> 00:06:19.078
[ Laughter ]

00:06:19.078 --> 00:06:20.345
And then everyone will go,
"Okay.

00:06:20.345 --> 00:06:21.814
I guess we'll pay for it then."

00:06:21.814 --> 00:06:23.482
[ Laughter ]

00:06:23.482 --> 00:06:24.884
-Yep. Hey, here's another.

00:06:24.884 --> 00:06:27.119
So we presented at the Emmys
this last year.

00:06:27.119 --> 00:06:28.988
-Yeah.
-And you have --

00:06:28.988 --> 00:06:31.257
This is how little you
like surprises or pranks.

00:06:31.257 --> 00:06:32.624
-That's right.
-You have a little trick.

00:06:32.624 --> 00:06:34.827
A backstage trick.
Because they give you

00:06:34.827 --> 00:06:36.462
the envelope, and then --
-Yeah, I hope I don't

00:06:36.462 --> 00:06:39.131
get in trouble for this because
we've hosted many things.

00:06:39.131 --> 00:06:41.934
But I like to look
and see who won.

00:06:41.934 --> 00:06:45.003
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:06:45.003 --> 00:06:48.740
-And by the way, I remember,
at the time,

00:06:48.740 --> 00:06:50.108
while you were like,
"You're allowed to check,"

00:06:50.108 --> 00:06:52.644
this was me.
-Yeah, you did not like it.

00:06:52.644 --> 00:06:54.180
And I was like, "Who cares?
What are they gonna do?

00:06:54.180 --> 00:06:55.781
Kick us out of here?"
-Yeah, exactly.

00:06:55.781 --> 00:06:57.449
-I was like --
And I was, like, checking.

00:06:57.449 --> 00:06:58.684
And if you squeeze sometimes,

00:06:58.684 --> 00:07:00.453
if you squeeze
the envelope like this,

00:07:00.453 --> 00:07:02.654
you can read the name, or you
can hold it up to the light.

00:07:02.654 --> 00:07:04.257
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:07:04.257 --> 00:07:06.192
-So I like to do that.
And we gave it to

00:07:06.192 --> 00:07:08.628
the well-deserving, amazing
Sheryl Lee Ralph.

00:07:08.628 --> 00:07:11.097
-Yeah, it was awesome.
-She was amazing.

00:07:11.097 --> 00:07:13.032
There she is.
-That is so fun.

00:07:13.032 --> 00:07:14.633
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:14.633 --> 00:07:19.004
But what I have found is,
when you know who's getting it,

00:07:19.004 --> 00:07:20.873
it's very hard
not to look at them.

00:07:20.873 --> 00:07:22.174
-Right.
[ Laughter ]

00:07:22.174 --> 00:07:23.943
-So I was like...

00:07:23.943 --> 00:07:25.411
[ Laughter ]

00:07:25.411 --> 00:07:26.979
"When I found out
it was Sheryl Lee Ralph,

00:07:26.979 --> 00:07:28.514
I was just staring
at Sheryl Lee Ralph like...

00:07:28.514 --> 00:07:30.383
[ Laughter ]

00:07:30.383 --> 00:07:32.151
"You got this.
You're gonna win."

00:07:32.151 --> 00:07:34.186
[ Laughter ]
I was like --

00:07:34.186 --> 00:07:36.088
I was like, "Get up!"

00:07:36.088 --> 00:07:37.657
[ Laughter ]
So I was like,

00:07:37.657 --> 00:07:39.392
"Ladies and gentlemen,
the winner is..."

00:07:39.392 --> 00:07:41.527
[ Laughter ]

00:07:41.527 --> 00:07:43.529
-Now every time
you present in the future,

00:07:43.529 --> 00:07:44.863
people are gonna know this,
and they're gonna --

00:07:44.863 --> 00:07:46.499
when you walk up, they're like,
"She already knows."

00:07:46.499 --> 00:07:47.899
-Yeah. Or --
-People are gonna be

00:07:47.899 --> 00:07:50.302
in the audience trying to make
eye contact with you.

00:07:50.302 --> 00:07:52.805
-But I do like -- I do like
knowing who's going to win.

00:07:52.805 --> 00:07:55.808
And I just like knowing just
one second before everyone else.

00:07:55.808 --> 00:07:57.043
-Yeah.
-You know what I mean?

00:07:57.043 --> 00:08:00.212
-[ Laughing ]
-Is that bad? Is that weird?

00:08:00.212 --> 00:08:01.981
-No, I think it's good.
-I mean, I like --

00:08:01.981 --> 00:08:05.117
What made me happy about it was,
when --

00:08:05.117 --> 00:08:08.153
Even though you know
there was one of six

00:08:08.153 --> 00:08:10.789
and you know all their names,
I'm so nervous

00:08:10.789 --> 00:08:12.291
that you're gonna screw up
the moment.

00:08:12.291 --> 00:08:14.793
So I like just like having
my lines a little bit earlier.

00:08:14.793 --> 00:08:16.529
-Exactly right.
Exactly right.

00:08:16.529 --> 00:08:17.796
And, you know,
you can change it.

00:08:17.796 --> 00:08:19.098
If you don't like the winner,
just change it.

00:08:19.098 --> 00:08:20.499
-That's the other rule
they don't know you can do.

00:08:20.499 --> 00:08:22.168
[ Laughter ]

00:08:22.168 --> 00:08:23.736
I remember. Remember,
they gave us the envelope,

00:08:23.736 --> 00:08:25.972
they go, "No peeking.
And also, say whoever you want."

00:08:25.972 --> 00:08:28.574
[ Laughter ]

00:08:28.574 --> 00:08:30.476
I want to ask about
your wonderful new show.

00:08:30.476 --> 00:08:32.879
We'll be right back with more
from Amy Poehler.

